# SORTING 

1. Selection sort

Problem Statement: Given an array of N integers, write a program to implement the Selection sorting algorithm.


Algorithm: start two fir loops, first from i =0 till i= n-1 to traverse the array and inner loop to find minimum.

Examples:

Example 1:
Input: N = 6, array[] = {13,46,24,52,20,9}
Output: 9,13,20,24,46,52
Explanation: After sorting the array is: 9, 13, 20, 24, 46, 52

#include<bits/stdc++.h>

using namespace std;
void selection_sort(int arr[], int n) {
  // selection sort
  for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {
    int mini = i;
    for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {
      if (arr[j] < arr[mini]) {
        mini = j;
      }
    }
    int temp = arr[mini];
    arr[mini] = arr[i];
    arr[i] = temp;
  }


2. Bubble Sort

void bubble_sort(int arr[], int n){
    //traversing array
    for(int i = n-1; i>= 1; i--){
        int DidSwap = 0;
        //swap
        for(int j=0;j<=i-1;j++){
            if(arr[j]> arr[j+1]){
                int temp = arr[j];
                arr[j]= arr[j+1];
                arr[j+1] = temp;
                DidSwap = 1;
            }
        }
        if (DidSwap == 0){
            cout<<"already sorted";
            break;
        }cout<<"swap done";
    }
}


